# Commit message prefixes

When creating a git commit in this workspace, **always** prefix the subject line with exactly one of these tags (including the colon):

`fix:` `feat:` `build:` `chore:` `ci:` `docs:` `style:` `refactor:` `perf:` `test:`

Choose the prefix from the **primary intent** of the staged changes. Inspect `git diff` and `git status` before writing the message.

## Prefix selection guide

| Prefix | Use when changes are mainly… |
|--------|------------------------------|
| `fix:` | Bug fixes, error handling, regressions, correcting broken behavior |
| `feat:` | New user-facing capability, API surface, or behavior |
| `build:` | Build tooling, bundlers, lockfiles, dependency manifests (`package.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `Cargo.toml`, `Makefile`, webpack/vite config) |
| `chore:` | Repo housekeeping with no product behavior change (`.gitignore`, editor config, scripts that aren’t CI/build/test/docs) |
| `ci:` | CI/CD pipelines (`.github/workflows/**`, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, CircleCI, Jenkinsfile, `codecov`, deploy workflows) |
| `docs:` | Documentation only (`README*`, `**/*.md`, `docs/**`, comments that document public API) |
| `style:` | Formatting, lint autofixes, whitespace, naming/style-only edits with **no** logic change |
| `refactor:` | Internal restructuring without changing external behavior |
| `perf:` | Performance improvements (caching, algorithms, query optimization) |
| `test:` | Tests only (`**/*.{test,spec}.*`, `**/__tests__/**`, `spec/**`, snapshots, fixtures for tests) |

## Mixed changes

- If multiple areas change, pick the **dominant** intent (what a reviewer cares about most).
- Prefer `feat:` or `fix:` over `chore:` when product code changes carry the main story.
- Do **not** combine multiple prefixes in one subject.

## Message format

```
prefix: Short imperative summary (≤72 chars)

Optional body explaining why, not just what.
```

## Examples

```
fix: handle null session in submission saver
feat: add paid diagnostic brief export
docs: update spec for black box engine
test: cover image upload validation paths
ci: run diagnostic suite on pull request
refactor: extract submission payload builder
```
